---
description: React feature composition and client integration
globs: "apps/web/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Route files compose small feature components. Keep page files under 200 physical lines and other source files under 300.
- Keep a feature's UI, queries, and mutations nearby. Add hooks only for real reusable state or behavior.
- `features/auth` holds shared session/password primitives (`Protected`, `PasswordField`, sign-out, cooldown). `features/auth-classic` holds compact AuthLayout UI (`AuthForm`, `AuthHeading`, Google button) used by `/signup`, verify-email, and password pages.
- SipNena onboarding lives under `features/onboarding|login|create-account` with thin route files. Prefer the shared onboarding shell + CSS tokens; keep si/ta/en string maps colocated.
- Full-bleed marketing/onboarding screens may sit on `rootRoute`. Compact verify/password pages stay on `authPage` + AuthLayout. Cookie auth mutations must still use `authClient` + HttpOnly cookies.
- Prefer Tailwind/CSS variables over inline `style=` (production CSP `style-src 'self'`). Self-host fonts used for Sinhala/Tamil (`font-src 'self'`). Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` for video and animation.
- Utilize horizontal space on portal/library UIs: content at least `max-w-7xl`, responsive grids that fill the width, gaps between items — not empty side gutters from a narrow max-width (see `layout-width.mdc`).
- Gate Google with `useAppConfig().googleEnabled`. Align password min length with Better Auth (8). Never fake sign-up success.
- Use the existing TanStack Router/Query setup and central HTTP error handling. Invalidate affected queries after successful mutations; avoid routine polling.
- Define route pages and authenticated/signed-out route layouts with `lazyRouteComponent` unless the component is required for the initial shell. Direct URL navigation, pending/error boundaries, and protected redirects must still work after splitting.
- Use relative `/api` URLs, Hono RPC for application data, and Better Auth's client for auth/organizations. Browser sessions use HttpOnly cookies; do not copy bearer tokens into browser storage.
- Provide loading, empty, error, and pending states. Prevent duplicate submissions and keep server authorization authoritative.
- Preserve semantic HTML, accessible labels, keyboard operation, and responsive layouts. Keep Tailwind's Vite integration working.
- E2E should use stable `data-testid`s (or updated product copy) when login/onboarding strings change.
- Run a production web build after route or dependency changes and compare initial minified and gzip sizes. Resolve large initial chunks through real route/component splitting before considering manual vendor chunks; do not raise `chunkSizeWarningLimit` merely to suppress a warning.
- Use real account and file data. Do not fill screens with invented metrics or infrastructure details.
